WEBVTT

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.770
Here it comes. Ready, Ray?

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.730
Yes, I'm ready. Come!

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:32.510
After the training...

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.270
...comes the protein!

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.110
So you're in two clubs at once?

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:39.520
Yeah.

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:41.890
I'm finally here at this academy.

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.020
I want to do everything I can.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.880
I see, but it's going to be rough.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.460
Don't worry about me.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:50.890
I've got this.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.030
Are you serious?

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:24.770
<b>The Iceblade <b>Sorcerer
</b>Shall <b>Rule </b>the <b>World</b></b>

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:27.000
<b>Episode 2
The Boy Who Became the World's Strongest Sorcerer
Begins His Practical Exercise</b>

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.720
Excuse me!

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:39.930
So you've come.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:42.260
My name is Ray White!

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:45.770
It seems you want to join our 
Environmental Research Club.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:47.220
The Environmental Research Club!

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.340
That means we explore the forests,

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:52.550
the rivers, all the way up 
to the glacier regions!

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:55.310
Those who conduct environmental 
research are fearless!

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:56.330
People call us...

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.580
...hunters!

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:01.070
We do not discriminate against ordinaries.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:04.160
However, a person with a 
weak body or a weak mind

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:06.010
cannot keep up with the 
Environmental Research Club.

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:07.590
Kinda scrawny.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.350
Not enough bulk...

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:14.810
Clothes off first!

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.010
Then we'll talk!

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:17.930
Yes, sir!

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.510
Bulk!

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.200
Check out that bulk!

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:30.410
I guess he just looks skinny in clothes!

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:33.960
He's huge! So huge he probably has 
to pay property tax on those!

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:35.490
Nice muscles.

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:36.850
They're not just for show, either.

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:39.770
You got them by actually using your body.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.610
I trained in the backwoods forests.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.920
So it's Ray, huh?

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:48.330
You have one of these, right?

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.010
You've got keen insight, sir.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:57.350
A gold hunter license?

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.780
An ordinary with a gold?!

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.310
Even amongst hunters,

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:01.830
a gold hunter is on another level!

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.090
But that makes sense then.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.380
That bulk is serious business!

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:09.110
Outstanding potential.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:18.340
Ray, become a pillar of the 
Environmental Research Club.

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:20.720
It would be my pleasure.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:31.330
Excuse me!

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:40.830
Oh, my. Ray?

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:43.830
You'd like to join?

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:44.610
Yes.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:47.590
I am interested in the plants 
that are living so powerfully.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.310
Even in the most appalling environment,

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.750
you can find a flower.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:56.230
Even if that's a battlefield.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.270
So you like flowers.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.280
I do.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.100
We don't have any other male members, though.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:06.040
Are you all right with that?

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.860
I have no problem communicating with women.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:09.970
Well, in that case...

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:11.520
I object!

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:14.400
Dina?

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:17.410
He's obviously set his sights on you!

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:20.310
We can't have a man step 
into the flower garden.

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:22.180
The flowers would wither.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:24.860
Not to mention, this person is an ordinary.

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:29.730
Then, let's do this.

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:32.530
I am delegating Ray's case to Dina.

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:33.680
Me?!

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:34.680
That's right.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:37.100
If you find that he's 
unworthy after your evaluation,

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.120
you can reject his application.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.200
U-Understood.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:42.600
Thank you very much!

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.190
Um...

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.650
My name is Dina Sera. I'm a third-year.

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:49.830
I look forward to working 
with you, Miss Sera.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:50.750
Harumph!

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:53.780
It's obvious that you'll reveal 
your true intentions soon enough!

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:58.700
You're going to prepare this space.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:01.490
So we're making a new garden.

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:02.600
That's right.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:05.220
It's nice that the academy 
let us use this space,

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:08.020
but it's full of weeds and the 
soil isn't workable yet, either.

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:09.220
We've got a long way to go.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.530
So is this my entrance test for the club?

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:12.980
You've got one week.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:14.410
And you've got to do it all by yourself.

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:15.550
Understood.

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:17.200
Good luck, then.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.890
Not that luck will help.

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:21.460
All right.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:22.460
Shall we begin?

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:13.490
This is looking good.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:15.240
You've been working really hard.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.010
This is delicious!

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:24.290
I'm glad.

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:27.110
I really love these fruit sandwiches,

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:30.080
so I negotiated with the school 
so we could have them.

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:32.090
It's possible to do something like that?

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:34.910
Well, I am the student council president.

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:39.020
You're from the top three families 
and the student council president.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.380
You are really amazing.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:43.780
If you ever have any questions, 
you can come to me.

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:53.430
Right, Magic Chevalier is coming up soon.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:55.270
Magic Chevalier?

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:59.790
It's a competition to find the 
strongest magic sword-fighter.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:01.530
The strongest... you said?

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:04.220
You're not going to participate?

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:06.570
I'll think about it.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.300
<i>Stare...</i>

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.430
Rebecca?

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:17.850
Do you mind if I touch them a little?

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:20.520
Go ahead.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:21.900
Very well.

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:26.320
Wow!

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:27.190
So hard!

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:30.240
Your biceps have an excellent 
shape and substance!

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:33.190
I trained in the backwoods forests.

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:34.580
That's amazing!

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:37.480
This is the first time I've 
touched a man's muscles.

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:38.580
It's really educational!

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.550
Isn't that the Withered?

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:42.310
I wonder if Lady Amelia alone is not enough,

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:45.230
so that's why he's trying to friendly with 
Rebecca from the top three noble families.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:48.670
Typical, perverted mindset of an ordinary.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.710
How did I do, Miss Sera?

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:00.490
...sed.

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:01.280
Huh?

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:02.560
You passed!

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:05.070
Thank you so much!

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:08.690
Then, let's plant some new flowers here.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:09.850
Yes!

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:20.080
Ray. I have something I'd like you to do.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:22.870
Let me have a look.

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:28.970
A spy from the empire inside the kingdom?

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:30.020
That is correct.

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:32.800
There is a chance that even this 
academy has been infiltrated.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:35.280
The staff has already been informed as well,

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:37.880
but if you find anything, let me know.

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:39.590
Yes, ma'am.

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:40.810
I apologize.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:44.100
But the state of affairs in the 
kingdom is quite messy right now.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:46.830
I'd like to resolve this 
in secret, if possible.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.090
Claris, is that you?

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:55.170
Ray?

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:58.480
Why would you suddenly talk to 
me like that? You startled me!

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:00.030
I apologize for that.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:02.860
But what are you doing here, 
crouched down like that?

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:06.700
I was watching some pill bugs.

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:07.510
Pill bugs?

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:11.930
I know it's weird for a high-class noble 
family's daughter to like insects.

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:16.960
Everyone else likes dogs or cats 
or some kind of cute animal.

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:19.460
That's why I don't have a lot of friends.

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:21.840
But that's part of who you are.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:23.490
I think that's really fantastic.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.130
You don't think it's weird?

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:27.110
I said I like bugs!

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:29.320
I like bugs too.

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:31.590
It is a great honor to be your friend.

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:33.570
F-friend?

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:38.370
D-d-d-did you s-say we're f-f-friends?!

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:39.700
I'm sorry.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:43.140
Somehow it seemed like we 
can talk so comfortably,

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:45.090
so maybe I read into it too far.

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:46.590
Did I offend you?

00:10:46.590 --> 00:10:49.170
A friend? I've never had...

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:51.870
I mean, if you want to. I guess.

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:53.620
Really? That would be nice.

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:56.740
All right! My very first friend!

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:58.540
I actually made a friend!

00:10:58.540 --> 00:10:59.630
What's wrong?

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:01.490
Nothing at all!

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:02.460
I see.

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:04.470
The sun's already starting to go down,

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:08.940
but I'd love to talk about the various 
bugs I saw in the jungle some time.

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:10.570
In great detail, you hear!

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:11.640
Promise!

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:13.340
It's a promise.

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:15.930
Besides, talking to you is a lot of fun.

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:19.490
I guess I have no choice.

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:22.370
Since you insist, I'll go along with it.

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:23.530
See you later.

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:27.970
I'm looking forward to it.

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:33.950
Today, we'll be talking about 
the derivations of sorcery.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:36.750
This topic is quite technical,

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:38.620
but is there anyone who 
can give an explanation?

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:40.130
Ray White.

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:41.410
How about you give it a try?

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:42.540
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:44.990
Sorcery is primarily 
categorized as low-grade,

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:47.390
mid-grade, high-grade, and holy-grade.

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:51.080
Furthermore: as quick,

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:53.460
remote,

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:56.390
chain,

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:00.610
delay,

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.170
material shift,

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:07.170
extensive,

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:12.160
extensive chain.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:15.170
The aforementioned are 
the seven derivations.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.020
White is absolutely right.

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:18.520
You've been studying hard.

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:19.530
Thank you.

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:30.060
That is all for today.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:34.220
Also, we'll be doing our practical 
exercise out in the Kafka Forest.

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:41.640
I want you to form groups 
of four before then.

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:42.400
That is all.

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:45.630
Yeah! For us that's easy!

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:47.000
Right, Al?

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:49.770
Lady Rose, will you be in our group?

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:51.390
Please, won't you?

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:52.490
What about being in our group?

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:56.470
What should I do?

00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:58.010
Let's group up, Ray.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:12:59.930
Is that okay?

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:02.940
It's common knowledge that 
I'm not great at sorcery.

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:04.990
You're good at using your body, right?

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:08.580
Besides, a gold hunter 
is worth 100 people.

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:10.660
Really? Well, thank you.

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:13.060
But what about the other spots?

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:22.500
Ray?

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:24.250
Elisa, want to be in our group?

00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:29.910
But... I mean...

00:13:30.190 --> 00:13:35.880
I'm happy, but I'm so physically 
weak that I'd just be a burden.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:36.910
Elisa...

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:42.290
Elisa, let's all do our best together.

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:43.820
We need you.

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:45.000
Ray.

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:47.470
I'll be supporting, too.

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:54.090
Okay. Thank you. Both of you.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.460
Do you still have an open spot?

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:05.020
Of course.

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:07.160
Your spot was there 
from the beginning.

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:23.920
Let's go over the details of 
this drill one more time.

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:28.570
The aim of this drill is to reach the 
goal in the center of the forest.

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:33.130
Do not forget to hit each checkpoint 
that are placed throughout the area.

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:37.190
The number stamps you collect 
will affect your final scores.

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:39.830
You have 24 hours.

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:41.490
Anything after that will not count.

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:47.380
The Kafka Forest is full of monsters that 
this unique environment has nurtured.

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:49.390
Be aware that combat will be necessary.

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:54.740
This will be the first practical 
exercise, but do not ask for help.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.750
That might lead to being held back a year.

00:14:57.400 --> 00:14:58.360
That is all.

00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:01.920
Wait at the designated area until 
the signal to start is given.

00:15:06.700 --> 00:15:08.060
I'm so nervous.

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:09.670
Don't worry, Elisa.

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:11.120
We're all here with you.

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:13.140
You're so kind.

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:15.610
You don't look nervous at all.

00:15:15.610 --> 00:15:16.670
Of course.

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:18.800
If anything, it's a nostalgic feeling.

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:19.880
Nostalgic?

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:21.690
I came from the middle of nowhere,

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:23.890
so I'm used to running around 
the forests and the mountains.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.730
Hey, what should we do about our order?

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:29.570
Right, we haven't decided that yet.

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:31.910
Maybe Ray and you should be the vanguard.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:34.930
I'll be in the middle and 
Elisa brings up the rear.

00:15:34.930 --> 00:15:36.290
That sounds good.

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:39.420
No, I'd like to take care 
of the middle, and help out as needed.

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:40.290
Huh?

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.570
I am used to these types of drills,

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:45.590
so I'd like you and Evi to be the vanguard.

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:50.880
That's fine, but what do you mean, 
you're used to these types of drills?

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:53.180
Let's just say, I learned a lot 
in those backwoods forests.

00:15:54.860 --> 00:15:56.430
It's time.

00:15:56.880 --> 00:15:59.040
The practical exercise will now commence.

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:01.730
You all ready?

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:02.470
Sure am!

00:16:02.470 --> 00:16:03.350
You bet!

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:05.730
I'll do my best.

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:06.610
I will do my best!

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:08.980
The exercise begins now!

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:35.880
Elisa, are you all right?

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:36.780
Ray!

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:37.490
All right!

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:39.220
So this is one of those monsters.

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:46.900
Wow.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.670
Split in two in one hit...

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:50.760
That's amazing. Ray!

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:52.600
Let's go.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:55.810
Hey, we found a stamp!

00:16:56.230 --> 00:16:57.580
Slap that on!

00:16:59.270 --> 00:17:00.480
All right!

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:01.550
We're doing great.

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:06.860
Are we even going the right way?

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:08.590
We are, I think...

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:10.250
Are you sure?

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:14.990
That's so huge!

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:23.280
We're making really good time.

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:25.600
At this rate, we could 
even make it back first.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.910
Ray was really amazing.

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:28.610
He was.

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:30.850
His battle abilities are exceptional.

00:17:31.140 --> 00:17:34.270
And he even has a wealth 
of survival knowledge.

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:36.670
That's what I'd expect from a gold hunter.

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:39.520
I came across many a monster 
in those backwoods forests.

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:42.130
So I'm used to this kind of situation.

00:17:42.130 --> 00:17:44.540
Backwoods forests, huh?

00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:48.400
She's doubting the "Universally applicable 
theorem of the backwoods forest"?

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:50.280
Master, you promised something else...

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:53.090
You're something different, huh Ray?

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:55.390
So are you, for that matter.

00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:57.080
I would've never expected the eldest daughter

00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:58.810
of the Rose family to align 
herself with an ordinary.

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:00.300
It's beyond weird.

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:04.090
I don't like that bloodline and class stuff.

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:06.800
The Rose family is the leader of the 
three big noble families, right?

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:08.090
Aren't you proud of that?

00:18:08.950 --> 00:18:11.160
I hate all of that formality.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:15.560
I mean, I've put in so much effort 
to become who I am right now.

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:17.820
Amelia?

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:20.380
It's fine.

00:18:20.380 --> 00:18:24.130
I'm really enjoying hanging out with 
you because you interact with me

00:18:24.130 --> 00:18:25.680
without all that formality.

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:28.830
I'm also happy that we're 
getting to know each other.

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:33.490
You really are too cute.

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:37.000
Cute all over!

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:38.850
Amelia, this is getting weird.

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:40.090
We're counting on you, Ray.

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:43.580
We're counting on you, Ray.

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:47.310
Compared to the battlefield,

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:49.060
this forest is heaven.

00:18:52.050 --> 00:18:55.360
Is it really okay for me to be here?

00:18:56.010 --> 00:18:59.350
Do I have the right to 
enjoy this kind of life?

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:00.770
Ray?

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:03.880
Is something wrong?

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:08.500
No.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:10.170
Let's get ready for tomorrow and go to bed.

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:28.800
Ray, I won't tell you to keep your 
identity hidden at all costs forever.

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:32.180
But your situation is quite special.

00:19:32.180 --> 00:19:34.770
If you want to enjoy a 
normal life at school,

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:37.150
it will be probably best to 
try to keep it under wraps.

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:43.250
However, if you ever find some friends 
that you can absolutely trust...

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:46.570
What should I do?

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:48.240
Master...

00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:55.640
What was that?

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:56.860
A scream?

00:19:57.690 --> 00:19:58.610
Hey!

00:19:58.610 --> 00:19:59.410
Ray, wait!

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:00.880
I'm sorry, I'm going ahead!

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:07.650
That scream just now. I have a bad feeling.

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:15.840
Help me!

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:17.350
Stay back!

00:20:17.350 --> 00:20:18.940
D-Damn it.

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:20.050
What the hell is going on?!

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:21.230
Mister Alium!

00:20:21.230 --> 00:20:22.590
Allow me to assist!

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:24.540
Withered?

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:26.850
Inside code, inertial control!

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:31.240
How is he moving like that?

00:20:53.510 --> 00:20:55.930
Can you stand, Mister Alium?

00:20:58.090 --> 00:21:00.240
Don't you dare look down on me!

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:02.750
You're just an ordinary!

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:04.900
I could've done that all by myself!

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:06.720
Oh, I see.

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:07.910
Did you have some kind of secret strategy?

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:10.820
You bastard!

00:21:10.820 --> 00:21:11.790
Ray!

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:16.080
What is that?

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:17.610
What a huge monster.

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:20.500
Mister Alium's party got attacked.

00:21:21.110 --> 00:21:24.290
Will you hurry up and get us down from here?

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:26.430
This hurts!

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:27.970
Hurry up!

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:31.050
Elisa, could I ask you to look after them?

00:21:31.050 --> 00:21:33.050
Yes, I got it!

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:34.320
I'll help, too.

00:21:36.990 --> 00:21:39.160
Did you defeat that by yourself?

00:21:40.620 --> 00:21:41.570
Yes, why?

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:44.730
Ray... who are you?

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:03.080
Hey, hey...

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:05.040
This can't be.

00:22:05.040 --> 00:22:06.370
Wha...

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:54.990
<b>The Iceblade <b>Sorcerer
</b>Shall <b>Rule </b>the <b>World</b></b>

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:54.990
<b>~ Next Episode Preview ~</b>

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:54.990
<b>~ Next Episode Preview ~</b>

